From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sat, 08 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] ZygoteProcess: Do not crash system_server when secondary
 zygote is absent

On a 64-bit-only GSI (init.zygote64.rc), the secondary 32-bit zygote
is never started. However, on devices like the Doogee Smini (MT6789)
the vendor partition still populates Build.SUPPORTED_32_BIT_ABIS,
causing bootCompleted() to attempt a connection to the nonexistent
secondary zygote socket. This throws an IOException that propagates as
a RuntimeException, fatally crashing system_server and triggering a
boot loop.

Catch the exception and log a warning instead, allowing the boot
sequence to complete. The primary 64-bit zygote is still notified
normally, and Vanadium (which only ships 64-bit libraries) continues
to work correctly under the 64-bit-only zygote configuration.

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000020
---
 .../java/android/os/ZygoteProcess.java        | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/java/android/os/ZygoteProcess.java b/core/java/android/os/ZygoteProcess.java
index 3ee18f5a7..b92c4e123 100644
--- a/core/java/android/os/ZygoteProcess.java
+++ b/core/java/android/os/ZygoteProcess.java
@@ -929,10 +929,20 @@ public class ZygoteProcess {
     private void bootCompleted(String abi) {
         try {
             synchronized (mLock) {
-                ZygoteState state = openZygoteSocketIfNeeded(abi);
-                state.mZygoteOutputWriter.write("1\n--boot-completed\n");
-                state.mZygoteOutputWriter.flush();
-                state.mZygoteInputStream.readInt();
+                try {
+                    ZygoteState state = openZygoteSocketIfNeeded(abi);
+                    state.mZygoteOutputWriter.write("1\n--boot-completed\n");
+                    state.mZygoteOutputWriter.flush();
+                    state.mZygoteInputStream.readInt();
+                } catch (ZygoteStartFailedEx ex) {
+                    // On 64-bit-only GSI builds the secondary 32-bit zygote is
+                    // intentionally not started, but the vendor may still list
+                    // 32-bit ABIs in Build.SUPPORTED_32_BIT_ABIS.  Do not crash
+                    // system_server when the corresponding socket is absent;
+                    // just log and continue.
+                    Slog.w(LOG_TAG, "Unable to notify zygote for ABI " + abi
+                            + " of boot_completed; socket may not exist", ex);
+                }
             }
         } catch (Exception ex) {
             throw new RuntimeException("Failed to inform zygote of boot_completed", ex);
-- 
